## Code review scope

**During code review, read only the standards sections that match files in the diff.** Do not load, skim, or apply standards from unrelated sections — even if you know them from memory.

### How to scope

1. Collect every file path under review (from the diff, PR, or an explicit directory such as `backend/`).
2. For each file, find every matching row in **Section map by changed file** below. **Union** all listed sections across all files.
3. Always include **General principles**, **Software design**, and **Review detection checklist**.
4. For each scoped section, open its **Rules file** from the **Section files** table below and read that file in full — not the entire standards tree.
5. Read the paired **examples** file(s) from the **Rule examples** table for each section you apply — not examples for sections you skipped.
6. When a finding maps to a standard, cite the **Standard** label from `skills/lmap-code-review/SKILL.md` and quote from that section's examples only.
7. Walk **every** row in **Review detection checklist** (`review-detection-checklist.mdc`) whose file-type column matches at least one file under review; report a finding for each hit (do not stop after security issues).

### Directory-wide review (no diff)

When the user asks to review a directory, package, or tree (e.g. "all files in `backend/`"):

1. Enumerate **all** source files under that path — PHP, Twig, JS, CSS, YAML config, migrations, Docker/compose, tests — not only recently changed files.
2. Union sections from **every** file using the section map; expect most sections to apply for a full Symfony backend.
3. Review **composed output** for Twig: mentally merge `extends` / `include` / `embed` chains (layout + page + partials) and flag duplicate landmarks, headings, and document shells.
4. Cross-check `config/packages/security.yaml` `access_control` and route `#[IsGranted]` attributes against every controller action that mutates data or exposes internal/admin/API surfaces.
5. Cross-check `phpunit*.xml` deprecation settings and `composer.json` / CI for dependency audit coverage.

For implementation tasks (not review), read the sections relevant to the files you are editing.

### Section map by changed file

Union every matching row for each changed file. A single file may match multiple rows (e.g. a Doctrine entity matches `.php` and Doctrine entities).

| Changed files | Sections to read |
|---------------|------------------|
| Any changed file | General principles, Software design, Review detection checklist |
| `.php` (when no more specific row below applies) | PHP, Security, Deployment and config (12-Factor) |
| `src/Helper/**`, `src/Util/**` | PHP, Security |
| `src/EventListener/**`, `**/EventListener/**` | Doctrine ORM, Symfony (incl. deprecations), Security |
| `.js`, `.ts`, `.mjs` | JavaScript, Security |
| `.js` using jQuery (`$`, `jQuery`) | jQuery, JavaScript, Security |
| `assets/**` (JS/CSS) | JavaScript, CSS, Symfony (AssetMapper), Security; add jQuery when `$`/`jQuery` appear |
| `.css`, `.scss`, `.sass` stylesheets | CSS, Security |
| Symfony controllers, services, `config/` | Symfony (incl. deprecations), Security, Deployment and config (12-Factor) |
| Symfony forms, translations (`translations/`) | Symfony (forms, i18n, deprecations), Security |
| `phpunit*.xml`, Symfony/Doctrine version bumps | Symfony (deprecations), Security |
| `tests/**` (functional, unit) | Symfony, PHP, Security |
| API controllers / API routes / `**/Controller/Api/**` | API endpoints, Symfony, Security |
| `.twig` templates | HTML in Twig templates, Twig, Symfony (template conventions) |
| `.twig` with PascalCase file/dir names (`ProductTile.html.twig`) | Symfony (template conventions), Twig |
| `.sql`, `**/migrations/**`, schema DDL | PostgreSQL |
| Doctrine entities, repositories, `Entity/` | Doctrine ORM, PostgreSQL, PHP, Symfony |
| `composer.json`, `package.json`, Docker, CI, `Dockerfile*` | Security (incl. CI audits), Deployment and config (12-Factor) |
| `*Controller.php`, `src/Input/**`, any PHP with `getEntityById` | LMAP |
| `compose.yaml`, `compose.*.yaml` | Security, Deployment and config (12-Factor) |
| Config / env files (`.env*`, `services.yaml`, etc.) | Security, Deployment and config (12-Factor) |

When reviewing a pull request (not just a local diff), also apply **General principles** bullets on commit/PR focus.

